ition (verified via `dladdr`), with a regression test.\n\n## Two things that go beyond output comparison\n\n**Guard pages** (`tests/phase_d_bounds.rs`): buffers are `mmap`ed flush against `PROT_NONE` pages so `dst + numElem` is the first unmapped byte. Value comparison cannot see an out-of-bounds *read*; this can.\n\n**Mutation testing** (`./mutation_check.sh`): 16 plausible mistranslations injected one at a time — **16/16 caught**. This mattered: changing the *scan* loop bound from `<` to `<=` is invisible to output comparison (all 200k fuzz cases still matched), and is caught only by the guard-page SIGSEGV. Without that test I'd have reported a false \"no divergence\" for that class of bug.\n\nReproduce with `cargo test --release`, `./run_all_configs.sh` (2 feature combos × 2 cdylib profiles, all green), `./mutation_check.sh`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":836,"cache_read_input_tokens":133539,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":836,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f09e42ff-20ef-4dfe-8256-475a7d13c8a1","uuid":"83a3beaa-5015-43a9-9017-865dbce8214b","timestamp":"2026-08-27T02:56:02.043Z"}
